# Units listed here are synced into /etc/systemd/system/ by
# scripts/deploy_server.sh on every deploy to main, and (for .timer/.path
# triggers only) enabled --now. This is a deliberate, explicit allowlist —
# NOT every file under deploy/systemd/ — because that directory also holds
# templated (@) units (qiniu-ssl-renew@.*) and manual/one-off or
# deferred units (e.g. wecom-thumbnail-backfill.service,
# wecom-message-purge.*, wecom-archive-reachability-check.*) that must
# never be auto-enabled.
#
# GH-104: this file is now a mechanical VIEW of deploy/systemd/
# WORKLOAD_MANIFEST — every row there with auto_install=true (and
# auto_enable=true for its .timer/.path member) belongs here, and nothing
# else does. WORKLOAD_MANIFEST is the authoritative classification
# (required / deferred / manual-oneshot / deprecated / static-helper /
# template / out-of-scope); this file stays a plain allowlist because
# that is all scripts/deploy_server.sh needs to parse. Read that manifest
# — not this comment — before adding, removing, or reclassifying a unit;
# backend/tests/test_gh104_scheduled_workload_reconciliation.py fails the
# build if the two ever disagree.
#
# To add a new auto-managed background job: add it to WORKLOAD_MANIFEST
# first, then list both its .service and its .timer/.path here. List the
# .service even though it is never enabled directly — it still needs to
# land in /etc/systemd/system/ for its .timer/.path to be able to trigger
# it. Units NOT listed here keep following the manual install steps in
# docs/DEPLOYMENT.md, or stay intentionally unmanaged per WORKLOAD_MANIFEST.
# GH-107: OnFailure= target for the units below. No .timer/.path partner —
# systemd instantiates it on demand, it is never `enable`d itself.
wecom-job-failure-alert@.service

wecom-archive-worker.service
wecom-archive-worker.timer
wecom-external-contact-reconcile.service
wecom-external-contact-reconcile.timer

# GH-104: incremental external-contact refresh. The .path is the PRIMARY
# low-latency trigger; the .timer is a boot + 15-minute retry/recovery
# fallback for a missed or failed path wake-up — both are required, they
# are not alternatives to each other.
wecom-external-contact-refresh.service
wecom-external-contact-refresh.path
wecom-external-contact-refresh.timer

# GH-104: generic media reconciliation. wecom-archive-media-event.path is
# the PRIMARY archive-complete signal; wecom-archive-media-download.timer
# is the 30-minute fallback/recovery cadence (RND-343 canonical design —
# do not shorten it back to the old 5-minute polling semantics). Both
# invoke the identical CLI entrypoint, so there is no risk of duplicate
# media records between the two triggers.
wecom-archive-media-event.service
wecom-archive-media-event.path
wecom-archive-media-download.service
wecom-archive-media-download.timer

